# interplay_diff_exec_opcodes: ExecIndirect2 (55) and ExecIndirect3 (67) run the same segments to the same bytes: the Workload steps, a double_gid dispatch and a copy, into a shared buffer each. Their resource records convert to the same flags: a private buffer listed with 55's bytes {0, 1, 1}, with {0, 3, 3} (each byte cut to its low bit), and with 67's flags 6 is synchronized back to the same bytes. InfoIndirect (69) decodes the same segments and never commits them: its buffer equals one nothing touched.
